From 477cc28786fb215e8f91250a2880fa11ad31bb6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:53:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: nt36536: report the pen tilt in the screen's axes

The controller reports the tilt along the screen's Y axis in byte 73
and the tilt along its X axis, with the sign inverted, in byte 74. The
driver used byte 73 for ABS_TILT_X and byte 74 for ABS_TILT_Y, so the
reported tilt was rotated by 90 degrees: tilting the pen up read as
tilting it left.

Report ABS_TILT_X from the negated byte 74 and ABS_TILT_Y from byte 73,
so that positive X tilts right and positive Y tilts towards the user.

Reported-by: vitalo233 <vitalo233@gmail.com>
Closes: https://github.com/joonhoekim/tb323fu-linux/issues/16
Suggested-by: vitalo233 <vitalo233@gmail.com>
Tested-by: vitalo233 <vitalo233@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>

y700 (kernel y18): upstream kernel-t58 patch 0153 (sha256
82e75995b4cb964c9456a31f21b8d4158b14552fc23381a7fbce12d65a64fde2),
the two changed lines byte for byte. Only the hunk's context differs:
upstream cut it against 0145 (pen reports outside the axes dropped),
which the y700 tree does not carry (no pen here; 0143/0145/0146 were
not taken, README upstream log 11-02); on t52's nt36xxx.c the two
lines follow pen_pressure directly. Not testable on this tablet (no
pen): carried for parity with upstream, pen path only.

y700 patch file: 0153-input-nt36536-report-the-pen-tilt-in-the-screen-s-ax.patch
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36536/nt36xxx.c
@@ -1017,8 +1017,8 @@ static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 				pen_x = (uint32_t)(point_data[67] << 8) + (uint32_t)(point_data[68]);
 				pen_y = (uint32_t)(point_data[69] << 8) + (uint32_t)(point_data[70]);
 				pen_pressure = (uint32_t)(point_data[71] << 8) + (uint32_t)(point_data[72]);
-				pen_tilt_x = (int32_t)point_data[73];
-				pen_tilt_y = (int32_t)point_data[74];
+				pen_tilt_x = -(int8_t)point_data[74];
+				pen_tilt_y = (int8_t)point_data[73];
 				pen_distance = (uint32_t)(point_data[75] << 8) + (uint32_t)(point_data[76]);
 				pen_btn1 = (uint32_t)(point_data[77] & 0x01);
 				pen_btn2 = (uint32_t)((point_data[77] >> 1) & 0x01);
-- 
